WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.150
The rabbis counted every
commandment in the Torah.

2
00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:05.560
They reached 613.

3
00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:08.270
248 tell you to do something.

4
00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:11.050
365 tell you not to.

5
00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:14.660
They reach into food,
family, business and courts,

6
00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:17.320
and even into how people care for animals.

7
00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:21.090
With so many commands, is
there any room left for choice?

8
00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:23.580
Are Jews still free to choose?

9
00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:26.510
In this mission, you'll sort
the mitzvot into groups,

10
00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:29.860
and meet two inner pulls
that every person feels.

11
00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:34.900
Then you'll compare which mitzvot Orthodox
and Reform Jews see as mattering most.

12
00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:40.520
Your mission: find out whether 613
commandments leave Jews free to choose.
